§ `ss 263 to 265 -- does Part 3.2 apply`

GIVEN w IS A `Where I first instructed the law practice`, sv IS A BOOLEAN, cn IS A BOOLEAN, ac IS A BOOLEAN, st IS A BOOLEAN, nt IS A BOOLEAN, ndate IS A DATE, tl IS A BOOLEAN, el IS A BOOLEAN, ch IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether Part 3.2 applies to my matter`
`applies` w sv cn ac st nt ndate tl el ch MEANS
    `ss 263 to 265 -- does Part 3.2 apply to my matter` w sv cn ac st nt ndate tl `1 Mar 2026` el ch

`ACT` MEANS `in the ACT`
`OTHER` MEANS `in another Australian jurisdiction`
`UNDECIDED` MEANS `it is not possible to decide where`

-- First instructed in the ACT: s 263.
#ASSERT `applies` `ACT` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3.2 applies: you first instructed the law practice in the ACT (s 263)`
-- Elsewhere, services mainly in the ACT, accepted a compliant written offer: s 264 (2) (a).
#ASSERT `applies` `OTHER` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3.2 applies: you accepted the law practice's written offer that it is to apply (s 264 (2) (a))`
-- Accepted the offer, but no ACT services or connection: s 264 (1) (b) fails.
#ASSERT `applies` `OTHER` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3.2 does not apply on these facts (the text's no: neither s 263 nor s 264 is met)`
-- The offer did not state what s 264 (3) requires, and no notification.
#ASSERT `applies` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3.2 does not apply on these facts (the text's no: neither s 263 nor s 264 is met)`
-- Cannot decide where; substantial connection; notified on day 28 after being told (1 Mar to 29 Mar): in time.
#ASSERT `applies` `UNDECIDED` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `29 Mar 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3.2 applies: you notified the law practice in writing that you require it to apply (s 264 (2) (b))`
-- Notified on day 29: no effect (s 264 (4)).
#ASSERT `applies` `UNDECIDED` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `30 Mar 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3.2 does not apply: your notification came more than 28 days after you were told of your right to give it, and has no effect (s 264 (4), the text's no)`
-- Never told of the right: the 28 days never start, so a notification on day 29 still takes effect.
#ASSERT `applies` `OTHER` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `30 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3.2 applies: you notified the law practice in writing that you require it to apply (s 264 (2) (b))`
-- First instructed in the ACT, matter now mainly elsewhere and the client chose the other law: s 265.
#ASSERT `applies` `ACT` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Part 3.2 has ceased to apply: the matter moved under another jurisdiction's corresponding law (s 265 (2)); costs incurred while it applied stay under it (s 268 (2))`
-- Mainly elsewhere, but no agreement or notification under the other law: s 263 still applies.
#ASSERT `applies` `ACT` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3.2 applies: you first instructed the law practice in the ACT (s 263)`
-- First instructed elsewhere and nothing else: no.
#ASSERT `applies` `OTHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3.2 does not apply on these facts (the text's no: neither s 263 nor s 264 is met)`

§ `ss 269 to 272 -- disclosure`

`DISCLOSE` MEANS `yes: in writing and in clear plain language, before or as soon as practicable after it is retained (ss 269, 271, 275), unless a regulation prescribes another exception (s 272 (1) (f), not deposited)`
`UNDER 1500` MEANS `no: the total legal costs are not likely to exceed $1 500, excluding GST and disbursements (s 272 (1) (a), the text's no); if the law practice becomes aware they are likely to, it must disclose as soon as practicable (s 272 (2))`

-- Exactly $1 500: "not likely to exceed" -- no disclosure needed.
#ASSERT `s 272 -- must my lawyer disclose the costs to me` 1500 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `UNDER 1500`
-- One cent over: disclosure.
#ASSERT `s 272 -- must my lawyer disclose the costs to me` 1500.01 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DISCLOSE`
-- Typical personal injury claim, $40 000 likely: disclosure.
#ASSERT `s 272 -- must my lawyer disclose the costs to me` 40000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DISCLOSE`
-- All three limbs of s 272 (1) (b).
#ASSERT `s 272 -- must my lawyer disclose the costs to me` 5000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you had a disclosure in the previous 12 months, waived further disclosure in writing, and a principal decided on reasonable grounds that it is not justified (s 272 (1) (b), the text's no)`
-- Waiver without the principal's decision: still disclosure.
#ASSERT `s 272 -- must my lawyer disclose the costs to me` 5000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DISCLOSE`
#ASSERT `s 272 -- must my lawyer disclose the costs to me` 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you are a client of a kind listed in s 272 (1) (c) (a sophisticated client; the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 272 -- must my lawyer disclose the costs to me` 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the costs, or how they are worked out, were agreed after a tender process (s 272 (1) (d), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 272 -- must my lawyer disclose the costs to me` 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: you will not be required to pay the costs and they will not otherwise be recovered, as in pro bono work (s 272 (1) (e), the text's no)`
-- Two exceptions at once: the first in the Act's order is given.
#ASSERT `s 272 -- must my lawyer disclose the costs to me` 1000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `UNDER 1500`

-- s 274.
#ASSERT `s 274 -- must I be told about the uplift fee` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 274 does not apply: the agreement has no uplift fee (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 274 -- must I be told about the uplift fee` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: before you enter the agreement, in writing, the uplift fee (or how it is worked out) and why it is justified (s 274 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 274 -- must I be told about the uplift fee` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: you are a sophisticated client (s 274 (3), the text's no)`

§ `s 277, s 278, s 279`

#ASSERT `s 277 -- what follows if my lawyer did not disclose` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 277 does not apply: the law practice disclosed everything required (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 277 -- what follows if my lawyer did not disclose` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you need not pay the legal costs, and the law practice cannot sue you for them, until they have been assessed (s 277 (1), (2)); on the assessment they may be reduced (s 277 (4)); you may also apply to set aside a costs agreement (s 277 (3))`
#ASSERT `s 277 -- what follows if my lawyer did not disclose` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the costs have been assessed: s 277 (1) and (2) no longer hold them back; the assessed amount may have been reduced for the failure (s 277 (4)); you may also apply to set aside a costs agreement (s 277 (3))`

#ASSERT `s 278 -- can I be charged for a report` `a report of the progress of the matter` EQUALS `you are entitled to it on reasonable request, in writing; the law practice may charge a reasonable amount for it (s 278 (1) (a), (2))`
#ASSERT `s 278 -- can I be charged for a report` `a report of the legal costs incurred to date, or since the last bill` EQUALS `you are entitled to it on reasonable request, in writing; the law practice must not charge you for it (s 278 (1) (b), (2), the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 279 -- on what basis can my lawyer charge me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `under your costs agreement (s 279 (a)), subject to Division 3.2.7 (costs assessment)`
#ASSERT `s 279 -- on what basis can my lawyer charge me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `in accordance with the applicable scale of costs (s 279 (b))`
#ASSERT `s 279 -- on what basis can my lawyer charge me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the fair and reasonable value of the legal services provided (s 279 (c))`

§ `s 282 -- form of the costs agreement`

`WRITTEN` MEANS `in writing, or evidenced in writing`
`BY CONDUCT` MEANS `by a written offer from the law practice that I accepted by conduct`
`ORAL` MEANS `orally, with nothing in writing`
`FORM OK` MEANS `yes, as far as s 282 goes`

#ASSERT `s 282 -- is my costs agreement in the required form` `WRITTEN` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `FORM OK`
#ASSERT `s 282 -- is my costs agreement in the required form` `ORAL` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a costs agreement must be written or evidenced in writing (s 282 (2), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 282 -- is my costs agreement in the required form` `BY CONDUCT` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an offer accepted by conduct must clearly state that it is an offer to enter a costs agreement, that it can be accepted in writing or by conduct, and what conduct is acceptance (s 282 (3), (4), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
-- s 282 (4) example: continuing to instruct after a proper offer.
#ASSERT `s 282 -- is my costs agreement in the required form` `BY CONDUCT` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `FORM OK`
#ASSERT `s 282 -- is my costs agreement in the required form` `BY CONDUCT` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a conditional (no-win no-fee) costs agreement must be signed by you, so acceptance by conduct is not enough (s 283 (3) (c) (iii), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
-- A sophisticated client need not sign (s 283 (5)).
#ASSERT `s 282 -- is my costs agreement in the required form` `BY CONDUCT` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `FORM OK`
#ASSERT `s 282 -- is my costs agreement in the required form` `WRITTEN` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a costs agreement cannot provide that the costs are not subject to costs assessment (s 282 (5), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
-- s 304A: a sophisticated client may contract out of assessment.
#ASSERT `s 282 -- is my costs agreement in the required form` `WRITTEN` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `FORM OK`

§ `s 283 -- conditional costs agreements`

`NEITHER` MEANS `neither a criminal proceeding nor a Family Law Act proceeding`
`CCA OK` MEANS `yes: it meets s 283 (2) and (3) as they apply to you`

#ASSERT `s 283 (2) -- is a no-win no-fee agreement allowed for my matter` `a criminal proceeding` EQUALS `no: not in a matter that involves a criminal proceeding (s 283 (2), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 283 (2) -- is a no-win no-fee agreement allowed for my matter` `a proceeding under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cwlth)` EQUALS `no: not in a matter that involves a proceeding under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cwlth) (s 283 (2), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 283 (2) -- is a no-win no-fee agreement allowed for my matter` `NEITHER` EQUALS `yes: a conditional costs agreement may relate to your matter (s 283 (2))`

-- Everything in place, cooling-off exactly 5 business days: meets s 283.
#ASSERT `s 283 (3) -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `NEITHER` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `CCA OK`
-- 4 business days: short.
#ASSERT `s 283 (3) -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `NEITHER` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it does not give a cooling-off period of at least 5 business days in which you may end it by written notice (s 283 (3) (e), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 283 (3) -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `a criminal proceeding` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: conditional costs agreements are not allowed in this matter (s 283 (2), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 283 (3) -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `NEITHER` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it does not set out what counts as a successful outcome (s 283 (3) (a), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 283 (3) -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `NEITHER` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it is not in writing (s 283 (3) (c) (i), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 283 (3) -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `NEITHER` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it is not in clear plain language (s 283 (3) (c) (ii), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 283 (3) -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `NEITHER` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you did not sign it (s 283 (3) (c) (iii), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 283 (3) -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `NEITHER` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it does not state that you were told of your right to seek independent legal advice before entering it (s 283 (3) (d), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`
-- Sophisticated client: no signature, no advice statement, no cooling-off needed (s 283 (5)).
#ASSERT `s 283 (3) -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `NEITHER` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CCA OK`
-- ... but it must still be in writing (s 283 (5) does not reach (c) (i)).
#ASSERT `s 283 (3) -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `NEITHER` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: it is not in writing (s 283 (3) (c) (i), the text's no); it is void (s 287 (1))`

§ `s 283 (3) (e), (6) -- cooling off (last day 10 March 2026)`

`CAN COOL OFF` MEANS `you can still end the agreement by written notice, up to and including the last day of its cooling-off period (s 283 (3) (e))`
`COOLED OFF` MEANS `you ended it in time: the law practice may recover only the costs of work done before you ended it, on your instructions and with your knowledge that it would be done in that period, and no uplift fee (s 283 (6))`
`TOO LATE` MEANS `too late: the cooling-off period has ended (s 283 (3) (e), the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 283 (6) -- can I still cool off` FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `10 Mar 2026` `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `CAN COOL OFF`
#ASSERT `s 283 (6) -- can I still cool off` FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `11 Mar 2026` `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `TOO LATE`
#ASSERT `s 283 (6) -- can I still cool off` TRUE `10 Mar 2026` `15 Mar 2026` `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `COOLED OFF`
#ASSERT `s 283 (6) -- can I still cool off` TRUE `11 Mar 2026` `15 Mar 2026` `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `TOO LATE`
#ASSERT `s 283 (6) -- can I still cool off` FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `1 Mar 2026` `10 Mar 2026` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no cooling-off right under s 283: you are a sophisticated client (s 283 (5), the text's no)`

§ `s 284 -- uplift fees (legal costs otherwise payable $20 000; 25% is $5 000)`

`UPLIFT OK` MEANS `allowed by s 284`

#ASSERT `s 284 -- is my uplift fee allowed` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 20000 EQUALS `s 284 does not apply: the agreement provides no uplift fee`
-- Exactly 25% in a litigious matter: allowed.
#ASSERT `s 284 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5000 20000 EQUALS `UPLIFT OK`
-- One cent over 25%: not allowed.
#ASSERT `s 284 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5000.01 20000 EQUALS `not allowed: in a litigious matter the uplift fee is more than 25% of the legal costs otherwise payable, excluding disbursements (s 284 (4) (b), the text's no); the agreement is void (s 287 (1)), and the uplift fee cannot be recovered and must be repaid if paid (s 287 (4))`
-- Not litigious: no 25% cap and no reasonable-belief test in s 284.
#ASSERT `s 284 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 9000 20000 EQUALS `UPLIFT OK`
#ASSERT `s 284 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 1000 20000 EQUALS `not allowed: in a litigious matter an uplift fee needs the law practice's reasonable belief that success is reasonably likely (s 284 (4) (a), the text's no); the agreement is void (s 287 (1)), and the uplift fee cannot be recovered and must be repaid if paid (s 287 (4))`
#ASSERT `s 284 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1000 20000 EQUALS `not allowed: the basis for working out the uplift fee is not separately identified (s 284 (2), the text's no); the agreement is void (s 287 (1)), and the uplift fee cannot be recovered and must be repaid if paid (s 287 (4))`
#ASSERT `s 284 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 1000 20000 EQUALS `not allowed: the agreement gives no estimate of the uplift fee, nor a range of estimates with the major variables (s 284 (3), the text's no); the agreement is void (s 287 (1)), and the uplift fee cannot be recovered and must be repaid if paid (s 287 (4))`
#ASSERT `s 284 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1000 20000 EQUALS `not allowed: the agreement is not a conditional costs agreement that meets s 283 (s 284 (1), the text's no); the agreement is void (s 287 (1)), and the uplift fee cannot be recovered and must be repaid if paid (s 287 (4))`

#ASSERT `s 284 (4) (b) -- the most uplift fee I can be charged` TRUE 20000 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 284 (4) (b) -- the most uplift fee I can be charged` TRUE 33000 EQUALS JUST 8250
#ASSERT `s 284 (4) (b) -- the most uplift fee I can be charged` FALSE 20000 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 285 -- contingency fees`

#ASSERT `s 285 -- is my agreement a prohibited contingency fee` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a contingency fee: s 285 does not prohibit it`
#ASSERT `s 285 -- is my agreement a prohibited contingency fee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `allowed: the part worked out from the award or settlement only adopts an applicable scale of costs (s 285 (2))`
-- "30% of whatever you recover": prohibited.
#ASSERT `s 285 -- is my agreement a prohibited contingency fee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `prohibited: the amount payable is worked out by reference to the award, settlement or property recovered (s 285 (1), the text's no); the agreement is void (s 287 (1)), the law practice can recover nothing for its services in the matter and must repay what you paid for them (s 287 (5))`

§ `s 287 -- void agreements (agreement $30 000 including a $5 000 uplift; fair value $28 000; paid $29 000)`

`NOT VOID` MEANS `it is not void`
`CONTINGENCY` MEANS `it is a prohibited contingency fee agreement (s 285)`
`UPLIFT BREACH` MEANS `it contravenes s 284 (uplift fees)`
`OTHER BREACH` MEANS `it contravenes another provision of Division 3.2.5 (for example s 282 or s 283)`

#ASSERT `s 287 -- the most my lawyer can recover under a void agreement` `NOT VOID` 30000 5000 28000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 287 -- what my lawyer must repay me` `NOT VOID` 30000 5000 28000 29000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 287 (5): nothing recoverable; everything paid comes back.
#ASSERT `s 287 -- the most my lawyer can recover under a void agreement` `CONTINGENCY` 30000 5000 28000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 287 -- what my lawyer must repay me` `CONTINGENCY` 30000 5000 28000 29000 EQUALS JUST 29000
-- s 287 (3), (4): the lesser of $28 000 and $30 000 - $5 000 = $25 000; repay $4 000.
#ASSERT `s 287 -- the most my lawyer can recover under a void agreement` `UPLIFT BREACH` 30000 5000 28000 EQUALS JUST 25000
#ASSERT `s 287 -- what my lawyer must repay me` `UPLIFT BREACH` 30000 5000 28000 29000 EQUALS JUST 4000
-- Fair value below the base costs: fair value governs ($20 000), repay $9 000.
#ASSERT `s 287 -- what my lawyer must repay me` `UPLIFT BREACH` 30000 5000 20000 29000 EQUALS JUST 9000
-- s 287 (2), (3): the lesser of $28 000 and $30 000; repay $1 000.
#ASSERT `s 287 -- the most my lawyer can recover under a void agreement` `OTHER BREACH` 30000 5000 28000 EQUALS JUST 28000
#ASSERT `s 287 -- what my lawyer must repay me` `OTHER BREACH` 30000 5000 28000 29000 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- Fair value above the agreement: capped at the agreement ($30 000); nothing to repay on $29 000 paid.
#ASSERT `s 287 -- the most my lawyer can recover under a void agreement` `OTHER BREACH` 30000 0 35000 EQUALS JUST 30000
#ASSERT `s 287 -- what my lawyer must repay me` `OTHER BREACH` 30000 0 35000 29000 EQUALS JUST 0

§ `s 288 -- setting aside`

#ASSERT `s 288 -- can I have my costs agreement set aside` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 288 does not offer this: you are not a party to a costs agreement with the law practice (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 288 -- can I have my costs agreement set aside` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `you may apply to the Supreme Court; on these facts it may set the agreement, or a provision of it, aside and fix fair and reasonable costs no greater than the agreement allowed (s 288 (1), (5) to (7))`
#ASSERT `s 288 -- can I have my costs agreement set aside` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `you may apply to the Supreme Court, but on these facts it would not set the agreement aside (s 288 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 288 (7) -- the most I can be ordered to pay after setting aside` 12000 10000 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `s 288 (7) -- the most I can be ordered to pay after setting aside` 8000 10000 EQUALS 8000

§ `s 281 -- interest (the section's own example: bill given 1 May 2008)`

`INTEREST 281 (1)` MEANS `yes: the costs have been unpaid for 30 days or longer after the day the bill was given, and the bill states that interest is payable and the rate; interest may run from the day after the bill was given (s 281 (1), (3))`

-- The example: unpaid on 1 June 2008, more than 30 days after the day of the bill.
#ASSERT `s 281 -- may my lawyer charge me interest` `1 May 2008` FALSE `1 May 2008` `1 Jun 2008` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `INTEREST 281 (1)`
-- 31 May 2008 is the 30th day after: not yet.
#ASSERT `s 281 -- may my lawyer charge me interest` `1 May 2008` FALSE `1 May 2008` `31 May 2008` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: the costs have not yet been unpaid for 30 days after the day the bill was given (s 281 (1))`
-- Paid on 31 May 2008: no interest under s 281 (1).
#ASSERT `s 281 -- may my lawyer charge me interest` `1 May 2008` TRUE `31 May 2008` `1 Jun 2008` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you paid by the 30th day after the day the bill was given (s 281 (1), the text's no)`
-- Paid on 1 June 2008: interest for the time it was unpaid.
#ASSERT `s 281 -- may my lawyer charge me interest` `1 May 2008` TRUE `1 Jun 2008` `1 Jun 2008` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `INTEREST 281 (1)`
-- The bill does not state interest and rate.
#ASSERT `s 281 -- may my lawyer charge me interest` `1 May 2008` FALSE `1 May 2008` `1 Jun 2008` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the bill does not state what s 281 (3) requires (the text's no)`
-- Under a costs agreement, with the bill stating all three things: from the start.
#ASSERT `s 281 -- may my lawyer charge me interest` `1 May 2008` FALSE `1 May 2008` `2 May 2008` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: under your costs agreement, as the bill states that interest is payable, the rate, and that it is payable under the agreement (s 281 (2), (3))`
-- Under a costs agreement, but the bill does not say it is payable under the agreement.
#ASSERT `s 281 -- may my lawyer charge me interest` `1 May 2008` FALSE `1 May 2008` `1 Jun 2008` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the bill does not state what s 281 (3) requires (the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 281 (4) -- the highest interest rate on my unpaid costs` 3.6 EQUALS 9.6
#ASSERT `s 281 (4) -- the highest interest rate on my unpaid costs` 0.1 EQUALS 6.1

§ `s 292 -- itemised bills (lump sum bill given 1 July 2026; day 90 is 29 September 2026)`

`LUMP` MEANS `a lump sum bill`
`ITEMISED` MEANS `an itemised bill`

#ASSERT `s 292 -- can I ask for an itemised bill` `LUMP` 5000 `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `29 Sep 2026` EQUALS `yes: ask by the last day, 90 days after the day the lump sum bill was given; the law practice must comply as soon as practicable and cannot charge for it (s 292 (3), (4), (8))`
#ASSERT `s 292 -- can I ask for an itemised bill` `LUMP` 5000 `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `30 Sep 2026` EQUALS `no: more than 90 days have passed since the day the lump sum bill was given (s 292 (3), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 292 -- can I ask for an itemised bill` `LUMP` 5000 `1 Jul 2026` TRUE `29 Sep 2026` `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS `you asked in time: the law practice must comply as soon as practicable and cannot charge for it (s 292 (4), (8))`
#ASSERT `s 292 -- can I ask for an itemised bill` `LUMP` 5000 `1 Jul 2026` TRUE `30 Sep 2026` `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS `no: more than 90 days have passed since the day the lump sum bill was given (s 292 (3), the text's no)`
-- Exactly $1 500: no right.
#ASSERT `s 292 -- can I ask for an itemised bill` `LUMP` 1500 `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `2 Jul 2026` EQUALS `no: the lump sum bill is for $1 500 or less, excluding GST and disbursements (s 269 (1) (c), s 292 (1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 292 -- can I ask for an itemised bill` `LUMP` 1500.01 `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `2 Jul 2026` EQUALS `yes: ask by the last day, 90 days after the day the lump sum bill was given; the law practice must comply as soon as practicable and cannot charge for it (s 292 (3), (4), (8))`
#ASSERT `s 292 -- can I ask for an itemised bill` `ITEMISED` 5000 `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `2 Jul 2026` EQUALS `s 292 does not apply: the bill is already itemised (the text's no: its "applies if" fails)`

#ASSERT `s 292 (3) -- the last day to ask for an itemised bill` `LUMP` 5000 `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS JUST `29 Sep 2026`
#ASSERT `s 292 (3) -- the last day to ask for an itemised bill` `LUMP` 1500 `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 292 (3) -- the last day to ask for an itemised bill` `ITEMISED` 5000 `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 289, 292 -- when the lawyer may sue (bill given 1 July 2026: day 30 is 31 July, day 90 is 29 September)`

-- Arguments: claim farming, bill given, kind, amount, asked for itemised, itemised given, itemised given on, disclosed,
-- assessed, assessment pending, leave to sue sooner, the day.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of bill`, amt IS A NUMBER, ask IS A BOOLEAN, given IS A BOOLEAN, givenOn IS A DATE, lv IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Whether my lawyer may sue me for the costs on that day`
`sue` kind amt ask given givenOn lv d MEANS
    `ss 289 and 292 -- may my lawyer sue me for the costs on that day` FALSE TRUE `1 Jul 2026` kind amt ask given givenOn TRUE FALSE FALSE lv d

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of bill`, amt IS A NUMBER, ask IS A BOOLEAN, given IS A BOOLEAN, givenOn IS A DATE, lv IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`earliest` kind amt ask given givenOn lv MEANS
    `ss 289 and 292 -- the earliest day my lawyer can sue me` FALSE TRUE `1 Jul 2026` kind amt ask given givenOn TRUE FALSE FALSE lv

`MAY SUE` MEANS `as far as Part 3.2 goes, yes`
`NOT BEFORE DAY 30` MEANS `no: not until at least 30 days after the day the bill was given (s 289 (1), the text's no)`

-- Itemised bill: day 29 (30 July) too early; day 30 (31 July) allowed.
#ASSERT `sue` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `30 Jul 2026` EQUALS `NOT BEFORE DAY 30`
#ASSERT `sue` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `31 Jul 2026` EQUALS `MAY SUE`
-- A proceeding started before the bill: too early.
#ASSERT `sue` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `30 Jun 2026` EQUALS `NOT BEFORE DAY 30`
-- Lump sum over $1 500: day 89 (28 September) too early, day 90 (29 September) allowed.
#ASSERT `sue` `LUMP` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `28 Sep 2026` EQUALS `no: not until at least 90 days after the day the lump sum bill was given (s 292 (6), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `sue` `LUMP` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `29 Sep 2026` EQUALS `MAY SUE`
-- Lump sum of $1 000: s 292 does not apply, only s 289.
#ASSERT `sue` `LUMP` 1000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `31 Jul 2026` EQUALS `MAY SUE`
-- Asked for an itemised bill, not given.
#ASSERT `sue` `LUMP` 5000 TRUE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS `no: you asked for an itemised bill and have not been given it (s 292 (7), the text's no)`
-- Itemised bill given 15 August: day 29 after it (13 September) too early, day 30 (14 September) allowed.
#ASSERT `sue` `LUMP` 5000 TRUE TRUE `15 Aug 2026` FALSE `13 Sep 2026` EQUALS `no: not until at least 30 days after the day the itemised bill was given (s 292 (7), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `sue` `LUMP` 5000 TRUE TRUE `15 Aug 2026` FALSE `14 Sep 2026` EQUALS `MAY SUE`
-- Leave to sue sooner (s 289 (2)) lifts the 30 days for an itemised bill ...
#ASSERT `sue` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` TRUE `2 Jul 2026` EQUALS `MAY SUE`
-- ... but not the 90 days of s 292 (6) (fork F6).
#ASSERT `sue` `LUMP` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` TRUE `2 Jul 2026` EQUALS `no: not until at least 90 days after the day the lump sum bill was given (s 292 (6), the text's no)`
-- The other bars.
#ASSERT `ss 289 and 292 -- may my lawyer sue me for the costs on that day` TRUE TRUE `1 Jul 2026` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS `no: the law practice is not entitled to recover any legal costs on the claim, because of a claim farming conviction (s 307A (2), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `ss 289 and 292 -- may my lawyer sue me for the costs on that day` FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS `no: it has not given you a bill complying with ss 290 and 291 (s 289 (1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `ss 289 and 292 -- may my lawyer sue me for the costs on that day` FALSE TRUE `1 Jul 2026` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS `no: the costs must first be assessed, because it did not make a disclosure required by Division 3.2.3 (s 277 (2), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `ss 289 and 292 -- may my lawyer sue me for the costs on that day` FALSE TRUE `1 Jul 2026` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS `MAY SUE`
#ASSERT `ss 289 and 292 -- may my lawyer sue me for the costs on that day` FALSE TRUE `1 Jul 2026` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS `no: a costs assessment has been applied for and is not completed (s 298 (b), the text's no)`

#ASSERT `earliest` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE EQUALS JUST `31 Jul 2026`
#ASSERT `earliest` `LUMP` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE EQUALS JUST `29 Sep 2026`
#ASSERT `earliest` `LUMP` 1000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE EQUALS JUST `31 Jul 2026`
#ASSERT `earliest` `LUMP` 5000 TRUE TRUE `15 Aug 2026` FALSE EQUALS JUST `14 Sep 2026`
-- Itemised bill given the same day as the lump sum bill: s 289's 30 days and s 292 (7)'s 30 days end together.
#ASSERT `earliest` `LUMP` 5000 TRUE TRUE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE EQUALS JUST `31 Jul 2026`
#ASSERT `earliest` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` TRUE EQUALS JUST `1 Jul 2026`
#ASSERT `earliest` `LUMP` 5000 TRUE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ss 289 and 292 -- the earliest day my lawyer can sue me` FALSE TRUE `1 Jul 2026` `ITEMISED` 5000 FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 294A -- time to apply for assessment (bill given 15 March 2026; last day 15 March 2027)`

GIVEN start IS A DATE, ap IS A BOOLEAN, apOn IS A DATE, td IS A DATE, li IS A BOOLEAN, te IS A BOOLEAN, co IS A BOOLEAN, cd IS A BOOLEAN, rl IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether I am in time to apply for a costs assessment`
`assess` start ap apOn td li te co cd rl MEANS
    `s 294A -- am I in time to apply for a costs assessment` start ap apOn td li te co cd rl

`IN TIME` MEANS `in time: you applied within 12 months (s 294A (5))`
`OUT OF TIME` MEANS `out of time: the Supreme Court may still deal with your application if, having regard to the delay and the reasons for it, it decides that is just and fair (s 294A (6))`

#ASSERT `assess` `15 Mar 2026` TRUE `15 Mar 2027` `15 Mar 2027` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `assess` `15 Mar 2026` TRUE `16 Mar 2027` `16 Mar 2027` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
#ASSERT `assess` `15 Mar 2026` FALSE `15 Mar 2026` `15 Mar 2027` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `still in time: you have until the last day, 12 months after the day the time began (s 294A (5))`
#ASSERT `assess` `15 Mar 2026` FALSE `15 Mar 2026` `16 Mar 2027` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- Applied before the bill day: counted as day 0, in time.
#ASSERT `assess` `15 Mar 2026` TRUE `14 Mar 2026` `16 Mar 2027` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- A sophisticated client out of time: no extension (s 294A (7)).
#ASSERT `assess` `15 Mar 2026` TRUE `16 Mar 2027` `16 Mar 2027` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `out of time, and as a sophisticated client you cannot have a late application dealt with (s 294A (7), the text's no)`
-- A consumer dispute not released (s 304), and one released.
#ASSERT `assess` `15 Mar 2026` TRUE `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no costs assessment: the costs are or were the subject of a consumer dispute under chapter 4 (s 304 (1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `assess` `15 Mar 2026` TRUE `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- Contracting out works for a sophisticated client only (s 304A).
#ASSERT `assess` `15 Mar 2026` TRUE `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs assessment: as a sophisticated client you contracted out of Division 3.2.7 (s 304A)`
#ASSERT `assess` `15 Mar 2026` TRUE `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- From 29 February 2024: the last day is 28 February 2025 (fork F9).
#ASSERT `assess` `29 Feb 2024` TRUE `28 Feb 2025` `28 Feb 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `assess` `29 Feb 2024` TRUE `1 Mar 2025` `1 Mar 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`

#ASSERT `s 294A (5) -- the last day to apply for a costs assessment` `15 Mar 2026` EQUALS `15 Mar 2027`
#ASSERT `s 294A (5) -- the last day to apply for a costs assessment` `29 Feb 2024` EQUALS `28 Feb 2025`
#ASSERT `s 294A (5) -- the last day to apply for a costs assessment` `31 Dec 2026` EQUALS `31 Dec 2027`

§ `ss 300C, 302 -- after the assessment`

-- $10 000 claimed, $8 500 assessed: cut by exactly 15%.
#ASSERT `s 302 -- who pays the costs of the assessment` 10000 8500 FALSE EQUALS `the law practice, unless the Supreme Court orders otherwise: the legal costs were reduced by 15% or more (s 302 (2) (a))`
-- $8 501 assessed: cut by 14.99%.
#ASSERT `s 302 -- who pays the costs of the assessment` 10000 8501 FALSE EQUALS `whoever the Supreme Court orders (s 302 (3))`
#ASSERT `s 302 -- who pays the costs of the assessment` 10000 8501 TRUE EQUALS `the law practice, unless the Supreme Court orders otherwise: it failed to comply with the costs disclosure rules of Division 3.2.3 (s 302 (2) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 302 -- who pays the costs of the assessment` 10000 10000 FALSE EQUALS `whoever the Supreme Court orders (s 302 (3))`

#ASSERT `s 300C (2) -- how much I can recover after the assessment` 10000 8000 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `s 300C (2) -- how much I can recover after the assessment` 5000 8000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 300C (3) -- the judgment against me after the assessment` 5000 8000 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `s 300C (3) -- the judgment against me after the assessment` 10000 8000 EQUALS 0

§ `s 307A -- claim farming`

#ASSERT `s 307A -- what my lawyer must repay me after claim farming` TRUE 4000 EQUALS JUST 4000
#ASSERT `s 307A -- what my lawyer must repay me after claim farming` FALSE 4000 EQUALS NOTHING
